1
00:00:01,333 --> 00:00:04,800
Real work in the middle: a worker, a site, a risk owner.

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:07,300
Priora places agents around it.

3
00:00:09,333 --> 00:00:13,933
WORKER (phone message): Hey, the bracket by the packing line has cracked again. We’re going to weld it before the night shift.

4
00:00:17,333 --> 00:00:19,967
Priora hears the job, and asks for a photo.

5
00:00:25,333 --> 00:00:29,267
Next, it summons only the specialists this site and job need.

6
00:00:33,333 --> 00:00:36,033
Each checks its own conditions and reports back.

7
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:42,200
When everything holds, the route opens.

8
00:00:42,667 --> 00:00:46,033
Work goes on, the record is kept, no one is disturbed.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,533
One condition slips: the fire watch is half the policy.

10
00:00:53,333 --> 00:00:55,200
Priora brings it to the risk owner.

11
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:58,200
Agents prepare, the human decides.

12
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:01,033
Retain is never a default.

13
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:05,100
Risk is kept on purpose, with its terms explicit.

14
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:12,067
Mitigate compares safeguards, and checks whether the work is back inside.

15
00:01:12,667 --> 00:01:17,633
Transfer, simulated for now, asks outside capacity for terms and a price.

16
00:01:18,667 --> 00:01:20,767
Priora carries the case between rooms.

17
00:01:21,333 --> 00:01:23,167
The risk owner stays in control.

18
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:32,767
Priora turns physical work into explicit risk decisions, while the work happens.
